! L.frr — Stub AS, customer of D
!
! L has a single upstream connection to provider D (10.1.7.2).
!
! As a stub, L:
!   - Announces only its own prefix (10.255.12.1/32) to D via the 'network' statement.
!   - Accepts all routes from D for global reachability.
!   - Provides no transit to any other AS.
!
! Money logic: L pays D for transit. D in turn pays A and B for global reachability,
! so L's traffic ultimately reaches the wider internet through the D→A/B path.

route-map FROM-PROVIDER permit 10
 set local-preference 100
!
router bgp __ASN__
 address-family ipv4 unicast
  neighbor 10.1.7.2 route-map FROM-PROVIDER in
 exit-address-family
!
